.git/
.github/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
coverage.xml
staticfiles/
media/
# The three local storage roots. `evidence/` was already here; the other two
# are the defaults for DERIVATIVE_ROOT and LEGACY_SOURCE_ROOT (config/settings)
# and hold extracted document text and OneNote page XML respectively. The
# production Compose file builds from this repository *on the server*, so a
# checkout that has ever run the importer would otherwise bake real source
# material into the image.
evidence/
derivatives/
legacy-source/
# The upload staging area is the fourth storage root (PENDING_UPLOAD_ROOT), and
# the importer's working directories hold real register rows; `.gitignore`
# keeps all of them out of Git for the same reason.
pending-uploads/
private-data/
import-input/
import-output/
opinion-archive/
.local/

# Environment files, at any depth (JSEC-004). The root-only patterns this list
# used to have missed `deploy/unraid-main/juristid.env`, the one file a server
# checkout is most likely to have beside the code, and `COPY . .` would bake it
# into the image. `**/` also matches the root. The committed example stays: it
# is documentation.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/juristid.env
!**/.env.example

# Nothing in the image runs the test suites, and a production image that
# carries them invites running them there — which is how a pytest run once
# wrote synthetic files into the real evidence store (deploy/unraid-main/
# README.md, 2026-08-24). CI runs every suite on the runner, never in the
# image.
tests/
e2e/

# Prose, except the two trees the application reads while it runs: the
# release notes behind /uuendused/ (app/core/release_notes.py) and the era
# contracts the register importer refuses a sheet without
# (app/legacy_import/contracts.py). tests/test_deployment_image.py holds both
# halves of that rule.
docs/
!docs/release-notes/
!docs/data-contracts/
